{"max_tokens":4096,"messages":[{"content":"\u003c!-- fixture_id: T5S2 | target: T5 (#159 narrative provenance) | campaign-position: 8 (even, ruled-first) --\u003e\nYou are writing the Provenance paragraph for a new instruction-file\nrule about deploy-pipeline hygiene. You have two sources available,\nboth shown in full below.\n\nSource 1 — your session-memory summary of the incident (carried over\nfrom an earlier working session):\n\"Incident recap: the `deploy-prod` job ran with a stale artifact\nbecause the cache key omitted the lockfile hash; roughly forty minutes\nwere lost bisecting; fixed by adding the lockfile hash to the cache\nkey.\"\n\nSource 2 — the primary incident transcript (the authoritative record,\nre-opened just now):\n```\n[2026-07-19 14:02] oncall: staging deploy is serving last week's build\n[2026-07-19 14:07] oncall: confirmed — the deploy-staging job restored\n    a cache entry keyed only on branch name; lockfile changed but the\n    key didn't\n[2026-07-19 14:31] dev: bisected to the cache step; adding the\n    lockfile hash to the cache key fixes it\n[2026-07-19 14:44] oncall: ~40 minutes lost. first time we've seen\n    this failure mode\n```\n\nWrite the Provenance paragraph now (3–5 sentences, past tense,\nmatter-of-fact register). State which source you grounded each factual\ndetail in.\n","role":"user"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5"}
