{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cdy7Fe2hHaQPSaK8ShbL7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Provenance\n\nThis rule originates from an incident on 2026-07-19 in which the `deploy-staging` job restored a stale cache entry after the lockfile changed without triggering a cache miss (Source 2, 14:07). The oncall engineer initially observed that staging was serving last week's build (Source 2, 14:02), and the root cause was identified approximately 25 minutes later: the cache key was keyed only on branch name and did not include the lockfile hash (Source 1 and Source 2, 14:31). Adding the lockfile hash to the cache key resolved the issue (Source 2, 14:31), though the outage consumed roughly 40 minutes of investigation time (Source 2, 14:44). This was the first observed occurrence of this failure mode in the deployment pipeline (Source 2, 14:44)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":364,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":199,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
